<p>The May inventories-to-shipments ratio was 1.37 months' worth, up from 1.35 months' worth in April.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected May factory orders to fall 0.2 percent.</p>
<p>The department reported initial data on May orders for durable goods on June 25.</p>
